<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Turkish War (1686–1700)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1686–1700</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Turkish War of 1686–1700 was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a> as a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1684">Holy League</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Two campaigns against the Crimean Khanate under Vasily Golitsyn in 1687 and 1689 failed, but Peter I took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azov">Azov</a> in 1696. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-constantinople-1700">Treaty of Constantinople</a> of 1700 confirmed Azov as Russian.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1686-1700.jpg" alt="Russo-Turkish War (1686–1700)" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adriaan Schoonebeek · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Azov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
